ros-jazzy-ros2-medkit-sovd-service-interface (0.7.0-1bookworm) bookworm; urgency=high

  * A cyclic-subscription request naming a resource path the collection cannot stream is refused instead of being accepted and never delivering
  * The sampler declaration stays inside the gateway, so the service interface no longer carries a second copy of it
  * Build and test only: the package is instrumented for coverage (#582 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/582>), and its tests take a DDS domain at run time from the shared allocator (#597 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/597>)
  * Contributors: @bburda

 -- "bburda" <bartoszburda93@gmail.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0000

ros-jazzy-ros2-medkit-sovd-service-interface (0.6.0-1bookworm) bookworm; urgency=high

  * ``list_entity_faults`` handles a fault ``status`` returned as an object (not just a string), supporting peer-fault aggregation across daisy-chained gateways (#419 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/419>)
